      <section id="CollegeDecisionLimitations" class="content-section">
        <h2>What these college calculators can and cannot answer</h2>

        <p>
          These calculators can organize tuition, living costs, borrowing, work income,
          and repayment pressure. They cannot guarantee admission, financial aid,
          transfer credits, graduation timing, job placement, or salary outcomes. Use
          the result as a financial pressure test, then confirm school-specific aid,
          program requirements, transfer rules, accreditation, job placement data, and
          repayment details.
        </p>

        <div class="college-hub-callout">
          <p>
            The safest college plan is not always the lowest sticker price. It is the
            path that keeps borrowing controlled, includes living costs honestly, gives
            the student a realistic path to finish, and still has a fallback plan if aid,
            work hours, or timing changes.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

